{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Also Judah</b> — After he mentioned Ephraim and set a harvest, like ועשה קציר (Joel 4:13) like נטע (planting). And the meaning: you set a harvest for yourself and aided the service of Baal in Bethel, when it was in my heart to restore the fortunes of my people, that they say: Come, let us return to YHWH. And on account of Judah, who abandoned my house and your aid, I will not restore your fortunes."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The Hebrew here is textually difficult: the syntax is compressed and elliptical, and the referents shift abruptly between second person and third person; rendered hyper-literally without smoothing."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:50:26.022814102Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}